        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Cost</strong> nothing · <strong>Requirements</strong> You are in <strong>Severance</strong></p><hr /><p><em>The Final Hour.</em> Respira stops being a breath and becomes a verdict.</p><p><strong>30-foot emanation</strong>, basic Fortitude, <strong>void</strong> damage.</p><p>Creatures that fail are <strong>enfeebled 3</strong> for 1 minute and <strong>drained 1</strong> for 24 hours as decades leave them.</p><hr /><p><strong>&#9888; Extrapolated</strong> &mdash; the aging is Baraggan's canon aspect of death.</p><hr /><p><strong>Waning.</strong> The damage is <strong>20d6</strong> if used in the first round of Severance, and two dice fewer each round after &mdash; 18d6, 16d6, 14d6, 12d6, 10d6, and <strong>8d6</strong> in the seventh. After the seventh round this cannot be used at all.</p><p><strong>Using this ends Severance</strong>, whether you want it to or not.</p>"
